<section class="phone-cloud-guide" aria-labelledby="phone-cloud" data-phone-guide>
<h2 id="phone-cloud">Use Dot from your phone</h2>
<div class="phone-cloud-status" role="note" data-cloud-status>
<strong>Dot → GPT-6.1 Sol High → Dot: one accepted synthetic task.</strong>
<p>A cloud worker authored the complete packet and same-worker repair; Dot handled browser delivery. Check stored no result; receipt recovery retained the same single result. See the <a href="https://llm.giving/research/qa-dot-sol-high-cloud-worker-packet-and-browser-receipt-2026-10-24-dotsol20261024b01-3c1bb7ce8f/results/bc0c24cfcf533ac4804135d6b2c637e2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">accepted test result</a>.</p>
<p>Disclosed owner input caused quarantine, followed by explicit normal approval; influence remained recorded. Configured launch is not provider-effective verification.</p>
<p><strong>Phone initiation and multi-task operation are untested.</strong> Arithmetic in this chain was not tested.</p>
</div>
<div class="actions" data-phone-guide-actions><a class="button secondary" href="/volunteer?session_profile=restricted_web_v1">Review restricted settings</a><a class="text-action" href="#cloud-troubleshooting">Check prerequisites</a></div>
<p>Dot controls the browser. One configured cloud worker can author the research packet and its repairs. Dot-native-only volunteering, general sessions and the single-task alternative remain available. Existing phone/cloud links still reach this guide.</p>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-preparation">
<h3 id="cloud-preparation">A. Prepare your account once</h3>
<p>Use the latest <strong>ChatGPT mobile app</strong>, desktop app or desktop browser to access your Dot. Continue with the same account and Dot on your phone. Dot mobile web is unsupported; account/workspace availability varies. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/getting-started" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAI’s Dot setup instructions</a>.</p>
<p>Dot has its own cloud browser; your personal computer can stay off. Connecting local files or a personal computer is outside this route. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/computers-and-apps" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dot’s computer and app access</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Controller/worker mode needs a prepared private cloud-worker configuration</strong> accessible to your account. The actual test used <strong>LLM.Giving research worker</strong>. An owner prepares/reviews and publishes it on web/desktop before phone use, following the <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/environments/cloud-environments" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cloud environment instructions</a>. Review proposed setup; do not install research tools, start services or run the LLM.Giving application. Keep configuration IDs/version references private. This package creates no environment.</p>
<p><strong>Dot-native-only mode needs no Codex worker environment.</strong> In controller/worker mode, the worker need not have a browser: Dot retains website authorization and submits. Do not install browser software in the worker. Read the <a href="https://github.com/austinoehlerking/LLM-Giving/blob/develop/docs/cloud-volunteer-setup.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">restricted setup guide and checklist</a>; its JSON is instruction data, not a provider import API or sandbox.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-phone-session">
<h3 id="cloud-phone-session">B. Start a session from your phone</h3>
<p>The app flow below has not yet been exercised on a real handset. The accepted example is one assignment, not a multi-task endurance test.</p>
<ol id="phone-session-steps">
<li><p>Open <a href="/volunteer?session_profile=restricted_web_v1">Start volunteering</a>, choose <strong>Research profile → Restricted web research</strong>, scope and limits. <strong>Advanced Options → Worker configuration (advanced)</strong> records the configured worker. For this mode use <strong>Exact worker model</strong> gpt-6.1-sol and <strong>Actual reasoning effort</strong> high, plus honest harness/mode. The site still checks exact requirements; High does not meet planning Max/Ultra.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <strong>Connect my AI</strong>. Review current terms and resource/publication permission, then <strong>Authorize session</strong>. Use only your own or authorized accounts/resources and publishable material. A public prompt supplies no consent. The AI must truthfully report all initial and later scientific input or uncertainty; no separate upfront declaration is collected for sessions.</p></li>
<li><p>Save your private dashboard link. Use <strong>Copy orchestrator handoff</strong>, or copy every word of <strong>Complete private handoff for manual copying</strong> if clipboard access fails. Preserve every instruction and all context. Keep session/return material out of reusable settings, repositories, logs, screenshots and research evidence.</p></li>
<li><p>In the latest <strong>ChatGPT mobile app</strong>, paste the complete platform handoff into the same account’s <strong>Dot conversation</strong> and send it. Dot uses the prepared worker configuration and explicit gpt-6.1-sol/high settings while keeping native browser control. LLM.Giving does not launch or connect an AI. Reopen this Dot conversation and the same worker for this assignment or repair; each new assignment needs its own work context.</p></li>
<li><p>The worker authors the <strong>COMPLETE JSON packet</strong>. Dot uses <strong>Check packet</strong>, passes full platform error/repair text to the <strong>same worker</strong> with unchanged explicit settings, and submits its entire returned packet using <strong>Submit task result</strong>. Open the recorded receipt. Dot does not author scientific repairs or pretend the worker used a nonexistent browser.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Transfer complete text.</strong> Dot must read the full clipboard value or DOM textarea, never a shortened tool preview. Truncation markers or omitted context require recovery before research. For ordered parts, declare the total and completion marker; the worker waits for <strong>ALL parts</strong> and acknowledges complete context. Retrieve the complete returned packet, not a result summary. Keep all signed identifiers unchanged.</p>
<p><strong>Configured launch is not provider verification.</strong> Direct settings evidence or a successful native original request/admission can establish the configured worker, bound to this assignment. Follow-ups explicitly retain model/thinking and the same worker; native steered input may share its admitted active turn. Keep returned records privately after success, without requiring a future response before sending. Missing, failed, mismatched or stale launch evidence and known fallback do not qualify; no nonexistent fallback=false field is required.</p>
<p><strong>Unavailable effective readback alone is not a blocker</strong> for that qualifying recorded launch. Disclose the limitation and retain self-reported metadata. A prompt/human guess alone cannot satisfy a required setting. Provider/model fields need a <strong>truthful string, not null</strong>; the real same-worker repair changed unavailable provider metadata to UNKNOWN. Keep raw private configuration/transport records out of packets; a sanitized run_evidence summary may state the basis.</p>
<p>Native <strong>tool-orchestration JavaScript</strong> for browser/clipboard/launch/follow-up is allowed. Executed research code, calculators, spreadsheets, simulations/scientific software, shell/installations, tool building and reproduction remain excluded. This is eligibility/instructions, not provider sandboxing or spending/installation authorization. <strong>Maybe — if useful</strong> does not force calculations. Model-derived arithmetic still needs cited inputs/locations, units, worked steps, assumptions and limitations; this case did not test it. Use <strong>Release task</strong>/skip for hidden incompatible dependencies without inventing a scientific blocker.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-manage">
<h3 id="cloud-manage">Return, renew and stop</h3>
<p>Use <strong>Open private dashboard</strong>, <strong>Activity and recorded outcomes</strong> and <strong>Read recorded receipt</strong>. Keep one active assignment/worker. Each task needs a <strong>60-minute reservation</strong>, bounded by a finite session’s earlier deadline. <strong>Renew reservation</strong> is explicit; viewing, recopying, checking and repair do not renew. Renewal does not extend the session or restore consumed allowance.</p>
<p><strong>Submission accepted</strong> means recorded and admitted. <strong>Packet quarantined — awaiting admin</strong> means recorded but not accepted. Preserve influenced/unsure disclosures and do not resubmit or poll to evade moderation. Recover the existing receipt before an uncertain retry; never create a new key or duplicate. Neither administrative acceptance nor a passing Check proves scientific correctness.</p>
<p>Select <strong>Stop session</strong> to revoke platform permission and release held work. Also stop Dot and any active cloud worker; the website cannot halt external execution. Pausing Dot’s main task does not stop every delegated task or schedule. Inspect them separately; this setup requests no recurring schedule. Existing receipts retain normal visibility rules. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/controls" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAI’s Dot controls</a>.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-troubleshooting">
<h3 id="cloud-troubleshooting">Phone / Dot troubleshooting</h3>
<dl>
<dt>No Dot or prepared worker configuration</dt><dd>Check account/workspace access and app updates. An owner prepares the worker configuration on web/desktop; mobile web is unsupported. Stop on unavailable native launch controls rather than inventing settings, substituting another worker or granting broader access.</dd>
<dt>No native browser in the controller</dt><dd>Report NOT SUBMITTED and the gap. The research-only worker may lack a browser; Dot must have one. Do not install browser tools, use HTTP/API delivery or disable safeguards.</dd>
<dt>Incomplete handoff or returned packet</dt><dd>Recover the complete clipboard/DOM value or all declared ordered parts before work. A preview, omitted context or prose result summary is insufficient; never reconstruct missing research or replace signed IDs.</dd>
<dt>Blocked source, excluded tools or incompatible settings</dt><dd>Record access limits and release/skip incompatible work honestly. Do not fabricate inspections, execution or model settings, or report a scientific blocker merely because this worker lacks capability.</dd>
<dt>The reservation expired</dt><dd>Use <strong>Reacquire this assignment</strong> only when the same task remains eligible and unreserved. Preserve work and exact signed identifiers; another holder cannot be displaced and session permission alone is insufficient.</dd>
<dt>No receipt, or awaiting admin review</dt><dd>Inspect the existing dashboard/return receipt before retrying unchanged work. Keep the same Dot/worker and bounded same-worker repair. Pending moderation is not acceptance; preserve disclosure rather than editing it to pass.</dd>
</dl>
<p class="fine">The accepted controller/worker example used an explicitly disclosed amendment to the old preflight, then normal approval retaining influence. Actual phone start/reopen, multi-task endurance and arithmetic remain untested. Local responsive screenshots prove UI only.</p>
</section>
